---
title: Incident Response Lifecycle
config:
    layout: elk
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> declared: alert / report triggers incident (external)

    declared --> triaging: IC claims incident

    triaging --> needs_diagnosis: IC assigns severity, assigns responder

    state "Diagnosis" as diagnosis_group {
        needs_diagnosis --> diagnosing: responder claims diagnosis
        diagnosing --> cause_identified: responder reports root cause
    }

    state "Mitigation" as mitigation_group {
        cause_identified --> mitigating: IC claims incident for mitigation
        mitigating --> needs_verification: IC requests verification (to process mitigation)
        needs_verification --> verifying: responder claims verification
        verifying --> cause_identified: responder reports mitigation failed
    }

    verifying --> stabilized: responder confirms production stable

    stabilized --> [*]: terminal (stabilized) — spawns postmortem (to process postmortem)

    note right of declared
        IC posts initial status update.
        Notifies PM at SEV-2+.
        Notifies PO at SEV-1.
    end note

    note right of triaging
        IC and responder must be different agents. Diagnosing and coordinating simultaneously produces bad outcomes.
    end note

    note right of diagnosing
        Consulting (architect, security) is informal during incidents. The responder stays in diagnosing while the IC coordinates consultant input via comments. No state change — the responder never hands off ownership, they get parallel assist.
    end note

    note right of mitigating
        IC decides strategy (rollback, flag toggle, or hotfix) and creates the necessary work items on the mitigation lifecycle. See mitigation-lifecycle for strategy-specific states.
    end note

    note right of cause_identified
        Mitigation failure loops back here, not to needs_diagnosis. Root cause is known — the strategy failed, not the diagnosis.
    end note

    note right of verifying
        Responder documents root cause as part of verification. By stabilized, root cause is already on the incident.
    end note

    note right of stabilized
        Terminal (stabilized). Production is stable; the incident is closed on this diagram. A new postmortem work item is spawned on the postmortem lifecycle. Follow-up issues are filed from that process, not this one.
    end note
